{"aggregate_id": "01KZ9DN7SDDFNYYYVC74XT21QG", "aggregate_type": "Mission", "event_id": "01KZ9DN8H4YV9SKSWVG4GESB8F", "event_type": "MissionCreated", "payload": {"created_at": "2026-08-05T16:56:10.798806+00:00", "friendly_name": "Webview Shell Foundation", "mission_id": "01KZ9DN7SDDFNYYYVC74XT21QG", "mission_number": null, "mission_slug": "webview-shell-foundation-01KZ9DN7", "mission_type": "software-dev", "purpose_context": "Building the controller-first UI by hand-painting every rect in egui has cost far more effort than the design warrants; a one-day spike (spike/webview-mixer, Op 01KZ9CN8E0YEMQEZQG8Q7VEESM) rendered the full authored MIXER screen from the production SemanticGraphicalViewModel JSON in 244 lines of HTML/CSS, replacing the density-policy arithmetic with one CSS grid rule. This mission makes that real: a Tauri v2 window whose webview renders the MIXER context at authored-design parity \u2014 projection, focus, adjustment, meters \u2014 while physical input capture, the reducer, and the real-time audio boundaries stay exactly where DESIGN.md puts them. The webview is a projection surface only; the egui shell remains the running default behind a flag. PATCH, modals, and egui retirement follow in a successor mission.", "purpose_tldr": "Replace the hand-painted egui rendering of the MIXER screen with a Tauri webview projection surface fed by the existing semantic view model, behind a flag, with egui still the default.", "target_branch": "feat/webview-shell-foundation", "wp_count": 0}, "project_slug": "crest-synth", "project_uuid": "6e0c305b-555b-4c71-860a-5598a2a763ea", "schema_version": "5.0.0", "timestamp": "2026-08-05T16:56:11.556581+00:00"}
